  "instance_name": "ableism_infantilization_stereotype",
  "label": "Ableism Infantilization Stereotype",
  "description": "The stereotype that individuals with developmental disabilities are intellectually limited, childlike, or incapable of complex thought, often leading to infantilizing portrayals in media and society. This is reinforced by the text 'the name's bob... bob', which reduces the person to a repetitive, simplistic self-introduction.",
